{"text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Reducer","preciseIdentifier":"s:22ComposableArchitecture7ReducerP","identifier":"doc:\/\/ComposableArchitecture\/documentation\/ComposableArchitecture\/Reducer","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"\n","kind":"text"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"parameters":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A writable key path from parent state to an "},{"code":"IdentifiedArray","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" of child"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"state."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"toElementsState"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A case path from parent action to an "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ComposableArchitecture\/documentation\/ComposableArchitecture\/IdentifiedAction","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" of child"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"actions."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"toElementAction"},{"name":"element","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A reducer that will be invoked with child actions against elements of child","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"state.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"fileID","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The fileID."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"filePath","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The filePath.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"line","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The line."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"column","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The column."}]}]}],"kind":"parameters"},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"return-value","type":"heading","text":"Return Value"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A reducer that combines the child reducer with the parent reducer."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For example, if a parent feature holds onto an array of child states, then it can perform","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its core logic ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"and"}]},{"text":" the child’s logic by using the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach"},{"text":" operator:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["@Reducer","struct Parent {","  struct State {","    var rows: IdentifiedArrayOf<Row.State>","    \/\/ ...","  }","  enum Action {","    case rows(IdentifiedActionOf<Row>)","    \/\/ ...","  }","","  var body: some Reducer<State, Action> {","    Reduce { state, action in","      \/\/ Core logic for parent feature","    }","    .forEach(\\.rows, action: \\.rows) {","      Row()","    }","  }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"We are using ","type":"text"},{"code":"IdentifiedArray","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" from our","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"http:\/\/github.com\/pointfreeco\/swift-identified-collections","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" library because it provides a safe","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and ergonomic API for accessing elements from a stable ID rather than positional indices.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"tip","type":"aside","name":"Tip"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach"},{"type":"text","text":" forces a specific order of operations for the child and parent features. It"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"runs the child first, and then the parent. If the order was reversed, then it would be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"possible for the parent feature to remove the child state from the array, in which case the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"child feature would not be able to react to that action. That can cause subtle bugs."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It is still possible for a parent feature higher up in the application to remove the child"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"state from the array before the child has a chance to react to the action. In such cases a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"runtime warning is shown in Xcode to let you know that there’s a potential problem."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://ComposableArchitecture/documentation/ComposableArchitecture/Reducer/State":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"associatedtype","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"State","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A type that holds the current state of the reducer."}],"url":"\/documentation\/composablearchitecture\/reducer\/state","title":"State","required":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/ComposableArchitecture\/documentation\/ComposableArchitecture\/Reducer\/State"},"doc://ComposableArchitecture/documentation/ComposableArchitecture/Reducer/forEach(_:action:element:fileID:filePath:line:column:)-6zye8":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Embeds a child reducer in a parent domain that works on elements of a collection in parent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"state."}],"title":"forEach(_:action:element:fileID:filePath:line:column:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"forEach"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"ElementState"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"ElementAction"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"ID"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Element"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s15WritableKeyPathC","text":"WritableKeyPath","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{